[{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00416.x","t":"Remoteness, Efficiency, Cost and the Reorganization of Scottish Local Government","a":["Edward C. Page","Arthur Midwinter"],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00416.x","pdf":"","k":["Politics","Administration (probate law)","Citation","Government (linguistics)","Local government","Library science","Public administration","Political science"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00417.x","t":"Public Participation in Bureaucratic Decision‐Making: A Reappraisal","a":["William P. Collins"],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"PUBLIC PARTICIPATION IN AGENCY DECISION MAKING: THE AMERICAN EXPERIENCE The materials listed deal with the normative and administrative dimensions of increasing the level of public participation in agency proceedings. Interesting, from the standpoint of the nuclear plant disaster at Three Mile Island, is Green's paper on licensing nuclear power plants; additionally, the 1972 Comment in the University of Pennsylvania Law Review is a superior description of the essential issues involved. THE PROBLEMS OF DELEGATION AND BUREAUCRATIC ACCOUNTABILITY: THE BRITISH EXPERIENCE Rosamund M. Thomas' The British Philosophy of Administration is an invaluable source here. Although Dr. Thomas focuses four seminal thinkers in this field, her thorough scholarship provides excellent entry points into this area. THE TRADITIONAL VIEW OF ADMINISTRATIVE LAW IN AMERICAN CONSTITUTIONAL THEORY The normal ‘transmission belt’ theory of public administration is given expression in the following texts. Louis Jaffe's book is perhaps the most rigorous and thorough. THE EXPANSION OF JUDICIAL STANDING The problems associated with expansion of judicial standing as it related to the expansion of the Administrative Procedures Act are given great attention in the legal literature. Davis' 1949 article should be compared to Jaffe's 1971 article for a perspective on how views shifted during that interval. Berger's article, in keeping with a reputation for fastidious legal scholarship, challenges the current trends toward the expansion of standing.","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00417.x","pdf":"","k":["Bureaucracy","Scholarship","Administrative law","Agency (philosophy)","Delegation","Political science","Public administration","Law"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00418.x","t":"Strengthening the Legislative Power of the Purse: The Origins of the 1974 Budgetary Reforms in the U.S. Congress","a":["John Dumbrell"],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00418.x","pdf":"","k":["Legislature","Citation","Politics","Power (physics)","Political science","Public administration","Library science","Law"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00415.x","t":"Policy Planning Units ‐ Ten Years On","a":["James Macdonald","Geoffrey K. Fry"],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00415.x","pdf":"","k":["Citation","Politics","Library science","History","Sociology","Political science","Media studies","Computer science"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00414.x","t":"Administrative Developments in 1979: A Survey","a":["David Steel","Jeffrey Stanyer"],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00414.x","pdf":"","k":["Politics","Citation","Library science","History","Political science","Law","Computer science"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00422.x","t":"Recent Government Publications","a":[],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00422.x","pdf":"","k":["Citation","Government (linguistics)","Computer science","Library science","Political science","Information retrieval","Linguistics","Philosophy"]},{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9299.1980.tb00420.x","t":"Book Notes","a":[],"d":"1980-12-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-929